# Title: Summarize the change
# - Imperative mood
# - Capitalize the first word
# - No period at the end
# - Maximum 50 characters
#
# Leave one blank line between the title and body.
#
# Body:
# - Explain what changed and why, not how.
# - Include the Jira issue/task ID.
# - Wrap lines at 70 characters:
# ################################################## which is here:  #
#
# Leave at least one blank line before the contributor section.
#
# Contributors:
# Include a Co-authored-by trailer for every contributor.
# Format:
# Co-authored-by: Name <user@users.noreply.github.com>
#
# Commit message guidelines:
# 1. Separate the subject from the body with a blank line.
# 2. Limit the subject to 50 characters.
# 3. Capitalize the subject line.
# 4. Do not end the subject with a period.
# 5. Use the imperative mood.
# 6. Wrap the body at 70 characters.
# 7. Explain what and why in the body, not how.
# 8. The # characters above are comments and are not part of the
# commit message. Remove them when writing the actual commit.
#
# Example:
#
# Fix checkout timeout on slow networks
#
# ABC-123: Increase the checkout timeout to prevent failures
# when requests take longer than the previous limit. This
# improves reliability for customers on slower connections.
#
# Co-authored-by: Jane Doe <jane.doe@users.noreply.github.com>
